// utf8_comment.edl  --  regression test for T-U01 / EdlScanner UTF-8 fix
//
// Before the fix, any non-ASCII byte in a comment (or anywhere in the input
// stream) would index the 128-entry yy_nxt transition table with a value in
// the range 128-255, producing undefined behaviour (typically a crash or
// garbage parse) on x86-64 Linux where plain char is signed.
//
// This file intentionally embeds non-ASCII UTF-8 sequences.  After the fix
// the scanner must parse this file without crashing, producing an empty
// object list (no top-level object declarations below).

// Example non-ASCII sequences that previously triggered the bug:
//   café     (UTF-8: 63 61 66 C3 A9 — 0xC3 and 0xA9 are > 127)
//   naïve    (UTF-8: 6E 61 C3 AF 76 65)
//   Müller   (UTF-8: 4D C3 BC 6C 6C 65 72)
//   résumé   (UTF-8: 72 C3 A9 73 75 6D C3 A9)
//   北京      (UTF-8: E5 8C 97 E4 BA AC — multi-byte CJK)

// The object list is intentionally empty so parsers that stop on error do
// not produce false positives from unrelated syntax issues.
